This fixture exercises a WordPress-shaped `wpdb` method that reaches phpc's
MySQLi statement data-seek handle validation. System PHP would require a real
mysqli statement object, buffered result cursor, and mysqlnd statement state;
phpc only records the reached non-statement-object diagnostic here. Supported
placeholder statement data-seek state is covered in later fixtures and does
not implement bound-result fetching, by-reference output-buffer mutation, real
cursor behavior, or host database state.
